OpenCLMath.scala third-party notices
===================================

The Scala adaptation was checked against the following files in musl 1.2.5:
  src/math/erf.c: erf, erfc, and their approximation coefficients
  src/math/lgamma_r.c: lgamma and logGammaPositive approximation coefficients
  src/math/tgamma.c: tgamma, gammaSeries, sinPiPositive, and Lanczos coefficients
  src/math/asinh.c, acosh.c, atanh.c: inverse hyperbolic formulas

gammaSign and the Scala control flow adapt these formulas to interpreter results.
The adaptation uses JVM/Scala Native math operations and explicit result values
instead of musl's floating-point exception-raising helpers.

Audited upstream archive:
  https://musl.libc.org/releases/musl-1.2.5.tar.gz
  SHA-256: a9a118bbe84d8764da0ea0d28b3ab3fae8477fc7e4085d90102b8596fc7c75e4

musl COPYRIGHT licenses the library under MIT and identifies the Sun math files
as separately permissively licensed. Its files without individual copyright
notices are covered by the library-wide copyright and permission notice.
Preserve the following notices with copies and distributions of this adaptation.

musl tgamma.c also credits these mathematical references and notes that its
ideas and constants draw on Boost and Python:
  "A Precision Approximation of the Gamma Function" - Cornelius Lanczos (1964)
  "Lanczos Implementation of the Gamma Function" - Paul Godfrey (2001)
  "An Analysis of the Lanczos Gamma Approximation" - Glendon Ralph Pugh (2004)

